% ============================================================================
% contraction.query.adj — a worked recall over the contraction library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does this
% contraction stand for?": it states no fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `contraction` rows and returns the
% expansion + the table's own source/locator/trust. A contraction the
% table does not carry abstains honestly — the engine never invents an
% expansion.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli contraction.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "contraction.adj"

? contraction(dont, $Expansion)     % expect do_not
? contraction($Word, will_not)      % expect wont
? contraction(shouldnt, $Expansion) % expect abstain -- no expansion is shipped for this contraction
